ity check compound into a result greater than any single\npass — and an eval that proves where the cascade leaks. Decisions confirmed with user:\n**full cascade** scope, fidelity judge is **advisory + best-wins** (never blocks ingestion).\n\n## Design (4 parts)\n\n### A. Whole-page substrate — `runtime/benny/core/docmodel.py`\n- **Persist per-page PNGs** when `emit_crops=True`: in `_extract_with_pymupdf`, render each\n  page (`page.get_pixmap(matrix=fitz.Matrix(2,2))`) to `.benny/docmodel/pages/<stem>/p{n}.png`.\n  Add a `pages: {page_no: ws_rel_path}` map to `_model_envelope`. Mirror in the docling\n  backend via `doc.pages[n].image` (already enabled by `generate_page_images`).\n- **Capture vector-drawing regions as crops.** After `table_rects`/`img_rects`, detect\n  vector clusters with `page.cluster_drawings()` (guarded; fitz ≥1.22). For each cluster\n  rect that passes area/aspect filters and isn't mostly inside a table/raster/text-dominant\n  region, render a clipped pixmap (`page.get_pixmap(clip=rect, ...)`), save as a crop, and\n  emit a `picture` element with `crop` set and a new `region: true` flag. Reuse\n  `_rect_mostly_inside` for overlap tests. This is what gives vector Databricks diagrams a crop.\n\n### B. Vision-grounded fidelity judge + cascade — `runtime/benny/core/vision_describe.py`\n- New `VISUAL_JUDGE_PROMPT` + `judge_visual_fidelity(...)` + `_parse_judge(...)`. The judge\n  is a **vision** call (it CAN see images), returning XML\n  `<judge><fidelity>0-10</fidelity><missing/><wrong/><extra/><verdict>faithful|partial|poor</verdict></judge>`.\n  Two modes (always-on, honest degradation):\n  - **Renderer available** (mmdc via existing `render_validate_mermaid`, which already returns\n    a PNG path): pass the **source crop + rendered-surrogate PNG** (+ page image for context)\n    so the VLM compares the diagram it produced against the original figure.\n  - **No renderer**: pass source crop (+ page) and the Mermaid **as text** in the prompt; VLM\n    still judges fidelity against the image. Keeps the review vision-grounded even in the bundle.\n- Rework `describe_element` diagram loop:\n  - New params: `page_bytes: Optional[bytes]=None`, `visual_judge: bool=True`,\n    `min_fidelity: float=7.0` (keep `render_check`).\n  - Optionally include `page_bytes` as a 2nd image on the **initial** describe call\n    (`vision_message(prompt, crop_bytes, page_bytes)`) for in-situ grounding.\n  - After each valid candidate, run the fidelity judge → record `visual_score`/`verdict`.\n    **best-wins now keys on `visual_score`** (then render-validity, then reviewer score).\n  - Refine prompt uses the **visual** critique (missing/wrong/extra from the judge) — the\n    \"another approach\" grounded in seeing both images. Break when `visual_score >= min_fidelity`.\n  - `validated = syntactically valid AND (visual_score>=min_fidelity OR judge unavailable)`.\n    Advisory: if no candidate hits threshold, still emit the highest-`visual_score` valid\n    diagram (never silently downgrade a real diagram to a caption); only `caption_fallback`\n    when nothing ever validated. Surrogate dict gains `visual_score`, `verdict`.\n- `classify_visual` gains `is_region: bool=False`; region crops in a technical doc default to\n  `diagram` (fixes the un-captioned-figure suppression). Pipeline passes the element `region` flag.\n\n### C. Pipeline wiring — `runtime/benny/core/vision_pipeline.py`\n- In `enrich_docmodel`, resolve each visual's page PNG from the docmodel `pages` map and pass\n  `page_bytes` + `visual_judge`/`min_fidelity` into `describe_element`; pass `is_region` from\n  the element. Extend `summary` with `visual_judged`, `avg_visual_score`, `faithful/partial/poor`,\n  `region_crops`. Add `visual_score` to the provenance comment in `_surrogate_to_markdown`.\n- `runtime/benny/api/vision_routes.py`: pass-through optional `visual_judge`/`min_fidelity` query params.\n\n### D. Eval harness — `runtime/scripts/vision_eval.py` (NEW)\n- CLI: `python scripts/vision_eval.py --workspace <ws> [--source <name>] [--min-fidelity N]`.\n- Builds/loads docmodels, runs the full cascade, and prints a **per-stage funnel**:\n  `visuals_total → crops_emitted (raster+region) → classified_diagram → mermaid_valid →\n  rendered_ok → fidelity≥threshold`, plus avg reviewer score, avg visual score,\n  caption_fallback rate, region-crop count.\n- Writes JSON + Markdown report to `.benny/docmodel/eval/`. Degrades honestly: if VLM/mmdc\n  absent, reports the structural funnel and flags the missing capability (no hollow success).\n\n### Tests\n- `tests/test_vision_describe.py`: `_parse_judge` XML parsing; best-wins-by-`visual_score`\n  selection with mocked `call_model`/renderer; degraded (no-renderer) judge path.\n- `tests/test_docmodel.py`: synthetic fitz PDF with a drawn rectangle → asserts a `region`\n  picture element + page PNG persisted.\n- `tests/test_vision_pipeline.py`: extend stitch tests for `visual_score` provenance + new summary keys.\n\n## Constraints honored\n- All model calls stay on `call_model()` (offline/lineage); artifacts stay **workspace-relative**\n  (like existing crops) — no absolute paths; every new step degrades gracefully (no hollow success).\n\n## Verification\n1. `cd runtime && pytest tests/test_docmodel.py tests/test_vision_describe.py tests/test_vision_pipeline.py -q`\n2. Offline funnel: `python scripts/vision_eval.py --workspace <ws>` → region crops > 0 on a vector page; funnel prints.\n3. With local VLM (Lemonade qwen3vl @127.0.0.1:13305) + mmdc installed, run eval against the\n   databricks workspace → expect `diagrams > 0` and a reported `avg_visual_score`; spot-check one\n   `*.enriched.md` Mermaid fence against the page PNG to confirm fidelity.\n\n## Files\n- Modify: `runtime/benny/core/docmodel.py`, `runtime/benny/core/vision_describe.py`,\n  `runtime/benny/core/vision_pipeline.py`, `runtime/benny/api/vision_routes.py`\n- Create: `runtime/scripts/vision_eval.py`\n- Tests: `runtime/tests/test